# What EAS Build is sent, and what it is not.
#
# The archive is taken from the repository root rather than from mobile/,
# because the app depends on ../packages/design by path — so everything else
# in this monorepo would ride along unless it is named here. The first upload
# came to 2.4 GB against a 2.0 GB limit.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file REPLACES .gitignore for the archive. Anything that must
# not leave this machine has to be named here as well, however thoroughly
# .gitignore already covers it. That is what the first block is.

# Never upload.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.p8
*.jks
*.keystore
**/secrets/

# Installed and generated on the build machine, not sent to it.
**/node_modules/
mobile/ios/
mobile/android/
mobile/.expo/
**/.expo-shared/

# The other halves of the product: a Go backend, a Vite site, an Electron app
# and the writing about all three. None of it is compiled into the phone app.
backend/
web/
desktop/
docs/
references/
.superpowers/
.claude/

# Build outputs and vendored SDKs that nothing in the app imports: previously
# built apks and ipas, the hardware handoff bundle, and the pendant's own iOS
# SDK. Nearly a gigabyte between them, and the archive is uploaded on every
# single build.
dist/
ios-sdk/
build-apk.sh
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
.playwright-mcp/

# Local noise.
.git/
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
